course: dictionary
lesson: 8131
title: Replace and its everyday meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To replace something means to put a new thing in the place of an old or broken one. «A helmet that has had a hard crash should be replaced, even if it looks fine.» The sentence tells you the old helmet goes and a new one takes its place.
explain: Replace can also mean to take someone's place. «Being short-staffed means people have left or are off sick and nobody has replaced them.» If nobody has replaced them, nobody has taken over their work. Use the swap check: put "take the place of" into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes replace means putting something back where it was. «Please replace the lid» means put the lid back on. The words around the word give you the clue, so you do not need to look it up every time.
fact: Replace means to put something new in the place of something old, or to put something back where it was.
fact: «Replace» can also mean to take someone else's place, as a substitute does when a tired player comes on.
fact: Replace, replaces, replaced and replacing are all forms of the same verb.
fact: «Sharks lose and replace thousands of teeth in their lives.» Replace here means a new tooth takes the place of an old one.
fact: In maths, «replace the letter with a number» means put the number in where the letter is, so you can work out the answer.
exercise: «Please replace the lid.» What does replace mean here? | Take it off and throw it away | *Put it back on | Lose it under the table | Paint it a new colour
exercise: A substitute can replace a tired player in a football match. What does replace mean? | *Take the player's place | Run faster than the player | Cheer loudly for the player | Hurt the player
exercise: «A helmet that has had a hard crash should be replaced, even if it looks fine.» Find and copy the word that means put a new one in the place of the old. | looks | *replaced | helmet | crash
test: «One robot replacing 10 packers takes jobs.» What does replacing mean in this sentence? | Packing boxes faster | *Taking the place of the packers | Repairing the packers | Trying to fix the robot
test: In 2 × n, replace n with 3. What do you get? | 5 | *6 | 4 | 9
exam: «Being short-staffed means nobody has replaced them.» What does replaced mean here? | *Taken the place of them | Moved them to a new room | Given them a prize | Hired a dog to help
